lis = '''    static int[] lisLengths(int[] a){int[] d=new int[a.length];Arrays.fill(d,1);for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++)for(int j=0;j<i;j++)if(a[j]<a[i])d[i]=Math.max(d[i],d[j]+1);return d;}'''
dpadd('Longest Increasing Subsequence', '''    public static int solve(int[] a){int[] tails=new int[a.length];int size=0;for(int x:a){int l=0,r=size;while(l<r){int m=l+(r-l)/2;if(tails[m]<x)l=m+1;else r=m;}tails[l]=x;if(l==size)size++;}return size;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{10,9,2,5,3,7,101,18}));','4',
    'Return length of a STRICTLY increasing subsequence, not necessarily contiguous.', 'tails[len-1] is the smallest attainable ending value of a subsequence of length len. Replacing a tail with a smaller value preserves length while helping future extension. Lower bound makes equality replace instead of extend.', 'O(n log n) time, O(n) space.', 'Tails evolve toward [2,3,7,18], giving length4.', 'The tails array itself need not correspond to one actual subsequence; reconstruction needs predecessors.')
dpadd('Print Longest Increasing Subsequence', '''    public static List<Integer> solve(int[] a){int n=a.length;int[] d=new int[n],parent=new int[n];Arrays.fill(d,1);Arrays.fill(parent,-1);int best=-1;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){for(int j=0;j<i;j++)if(a[j]<a[i]&&d[j]+1>d[i]){d[i]=d[j]+1;parent[i]=j;}if(best<0||d[i]>d[best])best=i;}List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();while(best>=0){out.add(a[best]);best=parent[best];}Collections.reverse(out);return out;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{10,9,2,5,3,7,101,18}));','[2, 5, 7, 101]',
    'Return one actual strictly increasing subsequence of maximum length, retaining first-found ties.', 'dp[i]=1+max dp[j] for j<i,a[j]<a[i]. Save the chosen predecessor and follow the best endpoint backwards to reconstruct.', 'O(n²) time, O(n) space.', 'At101, predecessor7 points to5 then2; reversing produces2,5,7,101.')
dpadd('Largest Divisible Subset', '''    public static List<Integer> solve(int[] input){int[] a=input.clone();for(int x:a)if(x<=0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();Arrays.sort(a);int[] d=new int[a.length],parent=new int[a.length];Arrays.fill(d,1);Arrays.fill(parent,-1);int best=-1;for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++){for(int j=0;j<i;j++)if(a[i]%a[j]==0&&d[j]+1>d[i]){d[i]=d[j]+1;parent[i]=j;}if(best<0||d[i]>d[best])best=i;}List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();while(best>=0){out.add(a[best]);best=parent[best];}Collections.reverse(out);return out;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,2,4,8}));','[1, 2, 4, 8]',
    'Positive integers; return a largest subset where every pair divides in one direction.', 'Sort and build a longest chain with a[i]%a[j]==0. Divisibility is transitive, so adjacent chain compatibility guarantees all pairs are compatible; reconstruct with predecessors.', 'O(n²) time, O(n) space.', '1 divides2 divides4 divides8, so all four fit.', 'Zero would make divisor remainder invalid; negative-divisibility ordering needs a different contract.')
dpadd('Longest String Chain', '''    public static int solve(String[] input){String[] a=input.clone();Arrays.sort(a,Comparator.comparingInt(String::length));Map<String,Integer> best=new HashMap<>();int answer=0;for(String s:a){int length=1;for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++){String prev=s.substring(0,i)+s.substring(i+1);length=Math.max(length,best.getOrDefault(prev,0)+1);}best.put(s,Math.max(length,best.getOrDefault(s,0)));answer=Math.max(answer,length);}return answer;}''','System.out.println(solve(new String[]{"a","b","ba","bca","bda","bdca"}));','4',
    'Each next chain word is formed by inserting exactly one character into its predecessor. Return maximum chain length.', 'Sort by length, then delete each character of a word to generate all possible predecessors. Their lengths are already processed; use the best chain stored by full string.', 'O(n log n+sum(wordLength²)) expected time due to string copying/hashing; O(total word characters) stored keys.', 'a->ba->bca->bdca has four words.', 'Equal-length words are not predecessors. Deleting from an empty string has no candidates but its own chain length is one.')
dpadd('Longest Bitonic Subsequence',lis+'''\n    public static int solve(int[] a){int[] up=lisLengths(a),down=new int[a.length];Arrays.fill(down,1);for(int i=a.length-1;i>=0;i--)for(int j=i+1;j<a.length;j++)if(a[j]<a[i])down[i]=Math.max(down[i],down[j]+1);int best=0;for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++)best=Math.max(best,up[i]+down[i]-1);return best;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,11,2,10,4,5,2,1}));','6',
    'A bitonic subsequence strictly increases then strictly decreases; either side may have length one.', 'At every peak i combine LIS ending at i and decreasing sequence starting at i; subtract one because peak is counted twice.', 'O(n²) time, O(n) space.', '1,2,10,4,2,1 has six values.', 'Some judges require both slopes nonempty; require up[i]>1 and down[i]>1 for that variant.')
dpadd('Number of Longest Increasing Subsequences', '''    public static BigInteger solve(int[] a){if(a.length==0)return BigInteger.ZERO;int[] length=new int[a.length];BigInteger[] count=new BigInteger[a.length];Arrays.fill(length,1);Arrays.fill(count,BigInteger.ONE);int best=1;for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++){for(int j=0;j<i;j++)if(a[j]<a[i]){if(length[j]+1>length[i]){length[i]=length[j]+1;count[i]=count[j];}else if(length[j]+1==length[i])count[i]=count[i].add(count[j]);}best=Math.max(best,length[i]);}BigInteger answer=BigInteger.ZERO;for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++)if(length[i]==best)answer=answer.add(count[i]);return answer;}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,3,5,4,7}));','2',
    'Count positional STRICT LISs of maximum length; empty input returns zero.', 'For each endpoint track best length and count. Better predecessor resets count; equal-best predecessor adds count. Finally sum counts at global-best endpoints.', 'O(n²) BigInteger additions; O(n) stored length/count states.', '1,3,5,7 and1,3,4,7 are the two length4 LISs.', 'Equal values do not extend an increasing sequence but distinct positions can give distinct length1 choices.')
lcs='''    static int[][] table(String a,String b){int[][] d=new int[a.length()+1][b.length()+1];for(int i=1;i<=a.length();i++)for(int j=1;j<=b.length();j++)d[i][j]=a.charAt(i-1)==b.charAt(j-1)?1+d[i-1][j-1]:Math.max(d[i-1][j],d[i][j-1]);return d;}
    public static int solve(String a,String b){return table(a,b)[a.length()][b.length()];}'''
dpadd('Longest common subsequence',lcs,'System.out.println(solve("abcde","ace"));','3',
    'Return length of longest common subsequence of two UTF-16 strings.', 'dp[i][j] uses prefixes of lengths i,j. Equal last characters extend dp[i-1][j-1]; otherwise skip one last character and take max(dp[i-1][j],dp[i][j-1]).', 'O(n*m) time/space; rolling rows can reduce auxiliary space to O(min(n,m)).', 'a,c,e match in order, though not contiguously, giving3.')
dpadd('Longest common substring', '''    public static int solve(String a,String b){int[] prev=new int[b.length()+1];int best=0;for(int i=1;i<=a.length();i++){int[] next=new int[prev.length];for(int j=1;j<=b.length();j++)if(a.charAt(i-1)==b.charAt(j-1)){next[j]=1+prev[j-1];best=Math.max(best,next[j]);}prev=next;}return best;}''','System.out.println(solve("abcdxyz","xyzabcd"));','4',
    'Longest common CONTIGUOUS substring length.', 'dp[i][j] is matching suffix length ending at these positions. Equal characters extend diagonal; a mismatch resets to zero. Maximize over all endpoints.', 'O(n*m) time, O(m) space.', 'abcd occurs contiguously in both strings with length4.', 'Unlike LCS, mismatches cannot inherit top/left values or contiguity would break.')
for title,insert in [('Longest palindromic subsequence',False),('Minimum insertions to make string palindrome',True)]:
    dpadd(title,lcs.replace('public static int solve(String a,String b)','static int common(String a,String b)')+'\n    public static int solve(String s){int length=common(s,new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString());return %s;}'%('s.length()-length' if insert else 'length'),
        'System.out.println(solve("bbbab"));','1' if insert else '4',
        'Return minimum insertions to make a palindrome.' if insert else 'Return longest palindromic SUBSEQUENCE length.',
        'The longest palindromic subsequence length equals LCS(s,reverse(s)); keeping it requires mirroring only the remaining n-LPS characters for the minimum-insertion problem.', 'O(n²) time/space in this LCS-table version.', 'bbbab has LPS bbbb length4; one inserted a can pair the unmatched a to make a whole-string palindrome.', 'Interview strings here are ASCII/BMP; surrogate-pair semantics need code-point adaptation. This computes a length, not arbitrary LCS reconstruction as a guaranteed palindrome.')
dpadd('Minimum insertions or deletions to convert string A to B',lcs.replace('public static int solve(String a,String b)','static int common(String a,String b)')+'''\n    public static int solve(String a,String b){return a.length()+b.length()-2*common(a,b);}''','System.out.println(solve("heap","pea"));','3',
    'Only insertions/deletions are allowed, not substitution; return minimum operations.', 'Keep an LCS unchanged. Delete n-LCS from a and insert m-LCS to reach b; any preserved sequence cannot exceed LCS, proving optimality.', 'O(n*m) time/space.', 'Keep ea; delete h,p from heap and insert p at front ->pea, three operations.')
dpadd('Shortest common supersequence',lcs+'''\n    public static String supersequence(String a,String b){int[][] d=table(a,b);int i=a.length(),j=b.length();StringBuilder out=new StringBuilder();while(i>0&&j>0){if(a.charAt(i-1)==b.charAt(j-1)){out.append(a.charAt(--i));j--;}else if(d[i-1][j]>=d[i][j-1])out.append(a.charAt(--i));else out.append(b.charAt(--j));}while(i>0)out.append(a.charAt(--i));while(j>0)out.append(b.charAt(--j));return out.reverse().toString();}''','System.out.println(supersequence("abac","cab"));','cabac',
    'Return a shortest string containing both inputs as subsequences; ties use the stated backtracking choice.', 'Backtrack LCS table. Equal characters are emitted once; otherwise emit the character from the side whose remaining LCS is longer. This shares exactly an LCS and gives length n+m-LCS.', 'O(n*m) time/space plus output.', 'cabac contains cab and abac in order, length5.', 'Shortest output need not be unique. The table backtrack determines one valid answer, not necessarily lexicographically smallest.')
dpadd('Distinct subsequences', '''    public static BigInteger solve(String source,String target){BigInteger[] d=new BigInteger[target.length()+1];Arrays.fill(d,BigInteger.ZERO);d[0]=BigInteger.ONE;for(char c:source.toCharArray())for(int j=target.length();j>=1;j--)if(c==target.charAt(j-1))d[j]=d[j].add(d[j-1]);return d[target.length()];}''','System.out.println(solve("rabbbit","rabbit"));','3',
    'Count positional subsequences of source equal to target; exact count, empty target one.', 'dp[j] counts matches of target prefix j. For each source character, matching positions add dp[j-1]; descend j so one source position cannot serve multiple target positions.', 'O(n*m) BigInteger additions, O(m) stored counts.', 'Choose any two of the three middle bs to form rabbit: three ways.')
dpadd('Edit distance', '''    public static int solve(String a,String b){int[] prev=new int[b.length()+1];for(int j=0;j<prev.length;j++)prev[j]=j;for(int i=1;i<=a.length();i++){int[] next=new int[prev.length];next[0]=i;for(int j=1;j<next.length;j++)next[j]=a.charAt(i-1)==b.charAt(j-1)?prev[j-1]:1+Math.min(prev[j-1],Math.min(prev[j],next[j-1]));prev=next;}return prev[b.length()];}''','System.out.println(solve("horse","ros"));','3',
    'Minimum unit-cost insert,delete,replace operations converting a to b.', 'Equal last characters cost no new operation; otherwise take1+min(replace diagonal,delete above,insert left). Empty-prefix cost equals its length.', 'O(n*m) time, O(m) space.', 'horse ->rorse (replace h), ->rose (delete r), ->ros (delete e): three.')
dpadd('Wildcard matching', '''    public static boolean solve(String text,String pattern){boolean[] prev=new boolean[pattern.length()+1];prev[0]=true;for(int j=1;j<prev.length;j++)prev[j]=prev[j-1]&&pattern.charAt(j-1)=='*';for(int i=1;i<=text.length();i++){boolean[] next=new boolean[prev.length];for(int j=1;j<next.length;j++){char p=pattern.charAt(j-1);next[j]=p=='*'?next[j-1]||prev[j]:(p=='?'||p==text.charAt(i-1))&&prev[j-1];}prev=next;}return prev[pattern.length()];}''','System.out.println(solve("adceb","*a*b"));','true',
    'Match the WHOLE text; ? matches one character, * matches any sequence including empty.', 'For *, either skip the star (current row left) or let it consume a text character (prior row same column). Other matches consume one character on each side.', 'O(n*m) time, O(m) space.', '* before a can match empty; middle * consumes dce; final b matches b.', 'This is wildcard matching, not regex; regex * repeats a preceding element instead.')
dpadd('Word Break', '''    public static boolean solve(String s,Set<String> words){boolean[] d=new boolean[s.length()+1];d[0]=true;int max=0;for(String w:words)max=Math.max(max,w.length());for(int end=1;end<=s.length();end++)for(int start=Math.max(0,end-max);start<end;start++)if(d[start]&&words.contains(s.substring(start,end))){d[end]=true;break;}return d[s.length()];}''','System.out.println(solve("leetcode",new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList("leet","code"))));','true',
    'Decide whether the whole string segments into reusable nonempty dictionary words; empty string succeeds.', 'dp[end] is true if some reachable prefix start precedes a dictionary suffix ending there. Bound search by longest word length.', 'O(n*L²) worst expected time including Java substring/hash costs; O(n+dictionary size) state.', 'dp[4] from leet is true; then code makes dp[8] true.', 'Empty dictionary tokens are ignored by the start<end loops. This returns existence, not every segmentation.')
dpadd('Count Palindromic Subsequences', '''    public static BigInteger solve(String s){int n=s.length();if(n==0)return BigInteger.ZERO;BigInteger[][] d=new BigInteger[n][n];for(int i=n-1;i>=0;i--){d[i][i]=BigInteger.ONE;for(int j=i+1;j<n;j++){BigInteger middle=j==i+1?BigInteger.ZERO:d[i+1][j-1];d[i][j]=s.charAt(i)==s.charAt(j)?d[i+1][j].add(d[i][j-1]).add(BigInteger.ONE):d[i+1][j].add(d[i][j-1]).subtract(middle);}}return d[0][n-1];}''','System.out.println(solve("aaa"));','7',
    'Count NONEMPTY positional palindromic subsequences, counting equal values at different indices separately. Exact BigInteger.', 'Different endpoints: add counts excluding either endpoint and subtract doubly counted middle. Equal endpoints: the newly wrapped middle subsequences and endpoint pair replace the subtraction, simplifying to left+right+1.', 'O(n²) BigInteger additions/subtractions and stored values.', 'aaa has three singletons,three pairs,and one triple =seven.', 'This is not count of distinct palindrome VALUES (aaa has only three distinct values). That variant needs next/previous equal-character bounds.')

dpadd('Matrix chain multiplication', '''    public static BigInteger solve(int[] dims){if(dims.length<2)return BigInteger.ZERO;for(int x:dims)if(x<=0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();int n=dims.length-1;BigInteger[][] d=new BigInteger[n][n];for(int i=0;i<n;i++)d[i][i]=BigInteger.ZERO;for(int len=2;len<=n;len++)for(int i=0;i+len<=n;i++){int j=i+len-1;for(int k=i;k<j;k++){BigInteger cost=d[i][k].add(d[k+1][j]).add(BigInteger.valueOf(dims[i]).multiply(BigInteger.valueOf(dims[k+1])).multiply(BigInteger.valueOf(dims[j+1])));if(d[i][j]==null||cost.compareTo(d[i][j])<0)d[i][j]=cost;}}return d[0][n-1];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{40,20,30,10,30}));','26000',
    'Matrix i has dims[i] x dims[i+1]; minimize scalar multiplication count, exact BigInteger.', 'For interval[i,j], split at every k; subinterval costs add dims[i]*dims[k+1]*dims[j+1]. Compute increasing interval lengths; singleton cost zero.', 'O(n³) BigInteger operations and O(n²) values.', 'Choose grouping ((A1*(A2*A3))*A4):6000+8000+12000=26000.')
dpadd('Burst balloons', '''    public static BigInteger solve(int[] values){int n=values.length;BigInteger[] a=new BigInteger[n+2];a[0]=a[n+1]=BigInteger.ONE;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){if(values[i]<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();a[i+1]=BigInteger.valueOf(values[i]);}BigInteger[][] d=new BigInteger[n+2][n+2];for(BigInteger[] row:d)Arrays.fill(row,BigInteger.ZERO);for(int len=1;len<=n;len++)for(int l=1;l+len-1<=n;l++){int r=l+len-1;for(int k=l;k<=r;k++){BigInteger cost=d[l][k-1].add(d[k+1][r]).add(a[l-1].multiply(a[k]).multiply(a[r+1]));d[l][r]=d[l][r].max(cost);}}return d[1][n];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{3,1,5,8}));','167',
    'Burst every nonnegative balloon, earning product of its current neighbors and itself; outside neighbor values one.', 'Choose the LAST balloon k in an interval so its outside neighbors remain fixed. Then solve independent left/right intervals and add the final product.', 'O(n³) BigInteger operations, O(n²) values.', 'Burst1 then5 then3 then8 in [3,1,5,8] earns15+120+24+8=167.', 'Choosing first makes changing neighbors entangle intervals; choosing last makes boundaries stable.')
pal_table='''    static boolean[][] palindromes(String s){int n=s.length();boolean[][] p=new boolean[n][n];for(int i=n-1;i>=0;i--)for(int j=i;j<n;j++)p[i][j]=s.charAt(i)==s.charAt(j)&&(j-i<2||p[i+1][j-1]);return p;}'''
dpadd('Palindrome partitioning II',pal_table+'''\n    public static int solve(String s){int n=s.length();if(n==0)return 0;boolean[][] p=palindromes(s);int[] parts=new int[n+1];for(int i=n-1;i>=0;i--){parts[i]=n;for(int j=i;j<n;j++)if(p[i][j])parts[i]=Math.min(parts[i],1+parts[j+1]);}return parts[0]-1;}''','System.out.println(solve("aab"));','1',
    'Minimum cuts partitioning the whole string into palindromic substrings; empty input zero.', 'Precompute palindrome intervals. parts[i]=min1+parts[j+1] over palindromic prefixes s[i..j]; number of cuts is parts-1.', 'O(n²) time/space.', 'aa|b uses two parts, hence one cut.', 'Subtract one only for nonempty strings; otherwise the empty suffix base would produce -1.')
dpadd('Partition Array for Maximum Sum', '''    public static long solve(int[] a,int k){if(k<1)throw new IllegalArgumentException();long[] d=new long[a.length+1];for(int i=a.length-1;i>=0;i--){long best=Long.MIN_VALUE;int max=Integer.MIN_VALUE;for(int j=i;j<a.length&&j-i<k;j++){max=Math.max(max,a[j]);best=Math.max(best,(long)max*(j-i+1)+d[j+1]);}d[i]=best;}return d[0];}''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,15,7,9,2,5,10},3));','84',
    'Partition all entries into blocks of length<=k; each entry in a block becomes the block maximum. Maximize total; negatives allowed.', 'For each start i try every allowed first-block endpoint j, track running maximum, and add its length*maximum plus optimal suffix dp[j+1].', 'O(n*k) time, O(n) space.', '[1,15,7]->45, [9]->9, [2,5,10]->30, totaling84.')
dpadd('Minimum cost to cut the stick', '''    public static long solve(int length,int[] input){if(length<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();int[] cuts=new int[input.length+2];cuts[cuts.length-1]=length;for(int i=0;i<input.length;i++){if(input[i]<=0||input[i]>=length)throw new IllegalArgumentException();cuts[i+1]=input[i];}Arrays.sort(cuts);for(int i=1;i<cuts.length;i++)if(cuts[i]==cuts[i-1])throw new IllegalArgumentException();long[][] d=new long[cuts.length][cuts.length];for(int span=2;span<cuts.length;span++)for(int l=0;l+span<cuts.length;l++){int r=l+span;d[l][r]=Long.MAX_VALUE;for(int k=l+1;k<r;k++)d[l][r]=Math.min(d[l][r],cuts[r]-cuts[l]+d[l][k]+d[k][r]);}return d[0][cuts.length-1];}''','System.out.println(solve(7,new int[]{1,3,4,5}));','16',
    'Cut a nonnegative length stick at distinct interior coordinates; each cut costs length of the current piece.', 'Sort cuts with endpoints0,length. Choose FIRST cut k of each interval: current length is paid once, then left/right pieces are independent. Compute increasing spans.', 'O(c³) time, O(c²) space.', 'Cut at3 costs7; optimal subpiece cuts total9; total16.', 'Do not confuse first-cut stick DP with last-burst balloons. This initial code rejects length0 even with no cuts due to duplicate endpoints; use positive length or the explicit no-cut fast path below.')
CONTENT['Minimum cost to cut the stick']['code']=CONTENT['Minimum cost to cut the stick']['code'].replace('if(length<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();','if(length<0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();if(input.length==0)return 0;')
CONTENT['Minimum cost to cut the stick']['pitfalls']='Distinct interior cuts are required. No cuts costs zero, including a zero-length stick. Use sorted coordinates and long aggregate cost.'
dpadd('Different Ways to Evaluate a Boolean Expression', '''    public static BigInteger solve(String s){if(s.isEmpty())return BigInteger.ZERO;if(s.length()%2==0)throw new IllegalArgumentException();int n=(s.length()+1)/2;BigInteger[][][] d=new BigInteger[n][n][2];for(int i=0;i<n;i++){char c=s.charAt(2*i);if(c!='T'&&c!='F')throw new IllegalArgumentException();d[i][i][0]=c=='F'?BigInteger.ONE:BigInteger.ZERO;d[i][i][1]=c=='T'?BigInteger.ONE:BigInteger.ZERO;}for(int len=2;len<=n;len++)for(int l=0;l+len<=n;l++){int r=l+len-1;d[l][r][0]=d[l][r][1]=BigInteger.ZERO;for(int k=l;k<r;k++){char op=s.charAt(2*k+1);if(op!='&'&&op!='|'&&op!='^')throw new IllegalArgumentException();for(int a=0;a<2;a++)for(int b=0;b<2;b++){int value=op=='&'?(a&b):op=='|'?(a|b):(a^b);d[l][r][value]=d[l][r][value].add(d[l][k][a].multiply(d[k+1][r][b]));}}}return d[0][n-1][1];}''','System.out.println(solve("T|T&F^T"));','4',
    'Operands T/F alternating binary &,|,^; count parenthesizations evaluating TRUE, exact BigInteger.', 'State(interval,truthValue). Split at every operator and combine all four left/right truth pairs, multiplying independent counts into the appropriate truth result.', 'O(n³) BigInteger multiply/add operations, O(n²) stored counts for n operands.', 'Four of the five parenthesizations of T|T&F^T evaluate true.', 'This counts parenthesizations, not assignments to variable symbols. Operator evaluation follows each chosen parenthesization, overriding ordinary precedence.')
